TI  - Parasites of the air passages.
PG  - 883-895
LID - S0012-3692(15)35961-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.13-2072 [doi]
AB  - Parasitic infestations affect millions of the world's population. Global 
      immigration and climate change have led to changes in the natural distribution of 
      parasitic diseases far removed from endemic areas. A broad spectrum of helminthic 
      and protozoal parasitic diseases frequently affects the respiratory system. The 
      wide varieties of clinical and radiographic presentations of parasitic diseases 
      make the diagnosis of this entity challenging. Pulmonologists need to become 
      familiar with the epidemiology, clinical presentation, pathophysiologic 
      characteristics, and bronchoscopic findings to provide proper management in a 
      timely fashion. This review provides a comprehensive view of both helminthic and 
      protozoal parasitic diseases that affect the respiratory system, especially the 
      airways.
