VI  - 146
IP  - 3
DP  - 2014 Sep
TI  - Mechanical circulatory support devices in the ICU.
PG  - 848-857
LID - S0012-3692(15)51089-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.13-2645 [doi]
AB  - The medical community has used implantable mechanical circulatory support devices 
      at increasing rates for patients dying from heart failure and cardiogenic shock. 
      Newer-generation devices offer a more durable and compact option when compared 
      with bulky early-generation devices. This article is a succinct introduction and 
      overview of the hemodynamic principles and complications after device 
      implantation for ICU clinicians. We review the concepts of device physiology, 
      clinical pearls for perioperative management, and common medical complications 
      after device implantation.
