TI  - A 54-year-old man referred with nonresolving pneumonia.
PG  - e92-e96
LID - S0012-3692(15)51099-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.13-2790 [doi]
AB  - A 54-year-old man was referred with nonresolving pneumonia. He had been treated 
      for community-acquired pneumonia 6 weeks earlier. He reported grade 2 dyspnea, 
      malaise, and a nonproductive cough. He had also experienced three episodes of 
      minimal hemoptysis but denied weight loss, fever, or any other constitutional 
      symptoms. He was a nonsmoker and was being treated for dyslipidemia.
