DP  - 2014 May
TI  - Symptom relief after large-volume thoracentesis in the absence of lung perfusion.
PG  - 1141-1143
LID - S0012-3692(15)34607-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.13-1523 [doi]
AB  - The physiologic basis for relief from dyspnea after therapeutic thoracentesis 
      remains poorly understood. Here, we describe the case of a 46-year-old man with 
      large recurrent pleural effusion with absent perfusion to the affected lung who 
      experienced dramatic dyspnea relief after large-volume thoracentesis. This 
      patient's improvement in breathlessness cannot be attributed to improved gas 
      exchange and suggests the primary physiologic basis for the relief in dyspnea is 
      a change in respiratory system mechanics or work of breathing.
