TI  - A case of pulmonary hemorrhage due to drug-induced pneumonitis secondary to 
      ticagrelor therapy.
PG  - 639-641
LID - S0012-3692(15)34379-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.13-1502 [doi]
AB  - We report a case of significant pulmonary hemorrhage developing shortly after 
      commencing ticagrelor and aspirin therapy and requiring coronary artery bypass 
      grafting to safely cease the antiplatelet therapy. Lung biopsy findings were 
      consistent with drug-induced lung injury. Clinicians should be aware of this 
      significant adverse event with this drug class.
