TI  - A 42-year-old farmer from Bangladesh with respiratory failure, septic arthritis, 
      and multiple cavitating consolidations.
PG  - e56-e59
LID - S0012-3692(15)48849-X [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.13-3000 [doi]
AB  - A 42-year-old man was directly admitted to the ICU with respiratory failure and 
      hypotension. Two weeks prior and just after returning from Bangladesh, he 
      presented to a polyclinic with fever, right knee pain, and generalized aches, for 
      which he received oral antibiotics. He was a farmer, had diabetes, never smoked, 
      and consumed alcohol occasionally.
