PG  - 1357-1370
LID - S0012-3692(11)60607-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.11-0295 [doi]
AB  - This is the third article of a three-part series that reviews the care of 
      poisoned patients in the ICU. This article focuses on natural toxins, such as 
      heavy metals and those produced by plants, mushrooms, arthropods, and snakes. The 
      first article discussed the general approach to the patient, including laboratory 
      testing; the second article focused on specific toxic agents, grouped into 
      categories.
