TI  - Beneficial effects of treatment with anti-IgE antibodies (Omalizumab) in a 
      patient with severe asthma and negative skin-prick test results.
PG  - 190-3
LID - 10.1378/chest.10-0128 [doi]
AB  - It is now well recognized that treatment with anti-IgE antibodies like omalizumab 
      is a valuable option in patients with allergic asthma who remain symptomatic 
      despite optimal treatment. To our knowledge, treatment with omalizumab in 
      patients with nonallergic asthma has not been reported. We present and discuss a 
      patient with severe asthma and elevated total IgE who had a negative 
      radioallergosorbent (RAST) test result and a negative skin-prick test result; the 
      patient showed a dramatic improvement with this treatment strategy.
