TI  - Diffuse alveolar hemorrhage.
PG  - 1164-71
LID - 10.1378/chest.08-2084 [doi]
AB  - Diffuse alveolar hemorrhage (DAH) is often a catastrophic clinical syndrome 
      causing respiratory failure. Recognition of DAH often requires BAL as symptoms 
      are nonspecific, hemoptysis is absent in up to one-third of patients, and 
      radiographic imaging is also nonspecific and similar to other acute alveolar 
      filling processes. Once the diagnosis is established, the underlying cause must 
      be established in order to initiate treatment. This review discusses the 
      diagnosis of the underlying histologies and the clinical entities that are 
      responsible for DAH as well as treatment options.
