TI  - Coagulopathy in critically ill patients: part 2-soluble clotting factors and 
      hemostatic testing.
PG  - 185-94
LID - 10.1378/chest.08-2535 [doi]
AB  - This manuscript provides an overview of how to interpret in vitro clotting 
      studies and how to select studies to evaluate patients with bleeding disorders in 
      the ICU. It provides a practical approach to understanding the complex subject of 
      clotting factor abnormalities, including the most common problems of 
      preanalytical error and anticoagulation therapy. Limitations and pitfalls of 
      diagnostic testing are highlighted.
