TI  - α1-antitrypsin deficiency: what has it ever done for us?
PG  - 1923-1929
LID - S0012-3692(15)48704-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.13-1901 [doi]
AB  - The first five cases of α1-antitrypsin deficiency were originally published in 
      1963. This changed our whole concept about the pathophysiology of emphysema, 
      including the role of inflammation and, in particular, the role of proteolytic 
      enzymes. However, the observation also had a significant 50-year impact on many 
      aspects of protein biochemistry, genetics, cell biology, and disease concepts 
      outside the lung as well as the study of COPD in general.
