TI  - The pros and cons of propensity scores.
PG  - 1380-1382
LID - S0012-3692(12)60667-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.12-1920 [doi]
AB  - Propensity scores have been proposed as a method of equating groups at baseline, 
      which is a problem, especially in studies that do not use randomization. This 
      article discusses some difficulties with the technique that may jeopardize the 
      findings if users (and readers) are not aware of these problems.
