TI  - Mammalian target of rapamycin inhibitors in organ transplantation: an unkept 
      promise.
PG  - 734-737
LID - S0012-3692(12)60519-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.12-1247 [doi]
AB  - The initial enthusiasm for the advent of a potentially nonnephrotoxic 
      immunosuppressant has been muted by data unmasking nephrotoxicity of mammalian 
      target of rapamycin inhibitors, including renal podocyte injury resulting in 
      proteinuria. Adverse reactions, including anemia, thrombocytopenia, 
      hyperlipidemia, and especially diabetogenesis, have limited its use to niche 
      indications such as prevention or amelioration of malignancy in organ transplant. 
      The class seems to be best used to address malignancy in organ allograft 
      recipients and as a first-line therapy in lymphangioleiomyomatosis.
