TI  - Toxicology in the ICU: Part 2: specific toxins.
PG  - 1072-1085
LID - S0012-3692(11)60548-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.10-2726 [doi]
AB  - This is the second of a three-part series that reviews the generalized care of 
      poisoned patients in the ICU. This article focuses on specific agents grouped 
      into categories, including analgesics, anticoagulants, cardiovascular drugs, 
      dissociative agents, carbon monoxide, cyanide, methemoglobinemia, cholinergic 
      agents, psychoactive medications, sedative-hypnotics, amphetamine-like drugs, 
      toxic alcohols, and withdrawal states. The first article discussed the general 
      approach to the toxicology patient, including laboratory testing; the third 
      article will cover natural toxins.
