TI  - Seizure-induced acute urate nephropathy: case report and review.
PG  - 666-669
LID - S0012-3692(13)60546-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.12-2129 [doi]
AB  - Urate nephropathy is observed primarily in patients treated for malignancy, but 
      several other predisposing conditions are recognized. We report a case in which 
      urate nephropathy complicated status epilepticus and review the literature 
      regarding previous similar cases. In addition, we discuss current views of the 
      pathophysiology of acute kidney injury due to urate nephropathy. This case 
      illustrates the value of carefully examining the urine of patients with acute 
      kidney injury to identify causes that may have a specific treatment.
