TI  - Coding and billing for home (out-of-center) sleep testing.
PG  - 539-543
LID - S0012-3692(13)60104-X [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.12-0425 [doi]
AB  - Obstructive sleep apnea is increasingly recognized as a comorbidity in many 
      medical illnesses. This has resulted in an increasing need for sleep testing, 
      which is not entirely met by the currently available sleep laboratory facilities. 
      Home, or out-of-center, sleep testing is an alternative to in-laboratory studies. 
      However, coding and billing for home studies is not as straightforward as it is 
      for in-laboratory studies. This article reviews the process of coding and billing 
      for sleep studies done in an unattended setting.
