TI  - Pulmonary alveolar proteinosis as a reaction to fentanyl patch smoke.
PG  - 1321-1323
LID - S0012-3692(12)60291-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.11-1462 [doi]
AB  - We report a patient who developed shortness of breath and systemic symptoms after 
      starting to smoke fentanyl patches. CT scan showed ground glass centrilobular 
      nodules, and biopsy demonstrated alveolar proteinosis. Her symptoms disappeared 
      and her chest imaging changes largely resolved when she stopped smoking the 
      patches. Alveolar proteinosis is an uncommon drug reaction and in this case 
      presented in a very unusual fashion as an inhalation injury.
