TI  - Assorted legal issues affecting medical practice.
PG  - 1190-4
LID - 10.1378/chest.09-2392 [doi]
AB  - The current article surveys an assortment of legal issues identified by the 
      editors that relate to the malpractice sphere. However, this represents only a 
      small part of the total legal medicine picture. The interaction of law and 
      medical care in the United States today encompasses a broad array of specific 
      points of contact between physicians' professional activities and various public 
      bodies and private entities. Several articles by other authors will appear in 
      subsequent issues of CHEST and flesh out much more comprehensively both the 
      topics outlined briefly here and other legal questions that concern contemporary 
      members of the medical profession.
