TI  - Novel asthma-associated genes from genome-wide association studies: what is their 
      significance?
PG  - 909-15
LID - 10.1378/chest.09-1554 [doi]
AB  - Asthma is a complex syndrome leading to the easily recognizable clinical feature 
      of wheezing. This is believed to be caused by inflammation, constriction of the 
      airway smooth muscles, and extensive mucus secretion. However, the mechanisms 
      initiating and maintaining these simple clinical features are not well 
      understood, even after 100 years of asthma research. Still worse is our 
      understanding of why certain individuals develop asthma and others do not.
