TI  - Advanced echocardiography for the critical care physician: part 1.
PG  - 129-134
LID - S0012-3692(15)49339-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.12-2441 [doi]
AB  - This is the first of a two-part series that reviews advanced critical care 
      echocardiography (CCE) techniques designed for critical care physicians. In this 
      section, we review training in basic and advanced CCE. This is followed by a 
      review of Doppler principles, including pulsed wave, continuous wave, and color 
      flow Doppler. Included are Doppler measurement techniques that are useful for 
      assessing the patient with cardiopulmonary failure and the common pitfalls of 
      Doppler. This section ends with a review of the quantitative and semiquantitative 
      measurements of stroke volume, as well as problems with measurement of stroke 
      volume in the ICU and its useful clinical applications. Video-based examples will 
      help demonstrate the techniques that are described in the text.
