TI  - An opportunistic infection associated with ruxolitinib, a novel janus kinase 1,2 
      inhibitor.
PG  - 1478-1479
LID - S0012-3692(13)60349-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.12-1604 [doi]
AB  - We report a case of Cryptococcus neoformans pneumonia in a patient taking 
      ruxolitinib, a janus kinase 1,2 inhibitor approved for the treatment of 
      myelofibrosis. We hypothesize that ruxolitinib contributed to this infection 
      through its effects on cell-mediated immunity. Clinicians should be aware of the 
      potential for intracellular or opportunistic infections associated with this 
      novel drug class.
