TI  - Severe pulmonary hypertension associated with emphysema: a new phenotype?
PG  - 1654-1658
LID - S0012-3692(12)60703-X [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.11-2816 [doi]
AB  - Mild to moderate precapillary pulmonary hypertension (PH) is a common 
      complication of COPD and has typically been related to severe airflow limitation 
      associated with chronic hypoxemia. Previous studies focusing specifically on 
      patients with emphysema found that worsening PH was associated with progression 
      of airflow obstruction. In the present report, we describe a new phenotype of 
      COPD with severe precapillary PH in patients presenting with progressive dyspnea, 
      normal spirometry, severely reduced diffusion capacity of the lung for carbon 
      monoxide, and high-resolution CT scans of the chest showing diffuse centrilobular 
      emphysema.
