TI  - Mine is bigger than yours: measures of effect size in research.
PG  - 595-598
LID - S0012-3692(12)60148-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.11-2473 [doi]
AB  - Results of studies that use laboratory tests are often easy to interpret, because 
      we are familiar with the units and how to interpret them. However, this is not 
      the case when the results are presented as ORs, relative risks, correlation, or 
      scores on an unfamiliar scale. This article explains these various indices of 
      effect sizes-how they are calculated, what they mean, and how they are 
      interpreted.
