TI  - Recent advances in testing for latent TB.
PG  - 1456-63
LID - 10.1378/chest.10-0366 [doi]
AB  - After more than a century of relying on skin testing for the diagnosis of latent 
      TB infection, clinicians now have access to blood-based diagnostics in the form 
      of interferon γ release assays (IGRAs). These tests are generally associated with 
      higher sensitivity and specificity for diagnosis of latent TB infection. This 
      article reviews the indications for testing and treatment of latent TB infection 
      in the overall context of a TB control program and describes how IGRAs might be 
      used in specific clinical settings and populations, including people having close 
      contact with an active case of TB, the foreign born, and health-care workers.
